      "body": "Hi @arista-nwolfe, I triaged this same thing. @arlakshm is tracking this with broadcom because ip_proto of 255 should be supported so the test shouldn't skip ip_proto of 255. Arvind could you share the BRCM ticket?"
    },
    {
      "author": "arista-nwolfe",
      "createdAt": "2024-12-04T00:36:18Z",
      "body": "> Hi @arista-nwolfe, I triaged this same thing. @arlakshm is tracking this with broadcom because ip_proto of 255 should be supported so the test shouldn't skip ip_proto of 255\r\n\r\nWhile searching broadcom cases for info on this I found `CS00012366805`.\r\nIn this case broadcom states that they are aware of this behavior and they intentionally moved it from next-header `252` to `255` in SDK `6.5.27`\r\n`It's a known issue fixed in 6.5.27. SW modified the default value to 255 in ucode source code.`\r\n\r\nMight be worth referring to this CSP for context in your conversation with BRCM @arlakshm "
    }
  ],
